{% comment %}
  Cart-drawer "You may also like" strip. Rendered from snippets/cart-drawer.liquid
  INSIDE <cart-drawer-items>, after </form> — see that file for why that node and
  no other survives every one of the drawer's re-render paths.

  There is no `section` object here: layout/theme.liquid:404 renders the drawer
  snippet straight into <body>, so section.settings and section.id are nil.
  Everything below comes from the cart or from settings.*.

  Cost, on EVERY template:
    - cart.item_count == 0 (most sessions) exits before any lookup;
    - a bag of 5+ lines exits too: the strip would leave under one cart line
      visible in the scroller, and a 5-line shopper is already converted;
    - the cart PAGE exits: it owns this job already (main-cart-items.liquid .rec),
      and a drawer add there would leave the page's own <cart-items> stale;
    - then <=3 cartel-pick-collection calls (handle + all_products_count only,
      never .products), and exactly ONE collection.products fetch, iterated at
      most 12 times, 3 cards maximum.

  Usage:
    {% render 'cartel-drawer-upsell' %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- if cart.item_count > 0 and cart.items.size <= 4 and request.page_type != 'cart' -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign up_want = 3
    assign up_deny = 'all, frontpage, best-sellers, best-selling-collection, new-collection, clearance'
    assign up_handle = ''

    # settings.cart_drawer_collection already exists in settings_schema.json
    # (Dawn ships it, this theme never referenced it) — a merchant override that
    # is already visible in the theme editor. A collection-type setting resolves
    # to a collection object, so read .handle and fall back to the raw value.
    assign up_prefer = settings.cart_drawer_collection.handle | default: settings.cart_drawer_collection
    if up_prefer != blank
      assign up_handle = up_prefer
    else
      # cart.items is ordered by first-add, so reversing puts the newest line
      # first and the strip follows what the shopper most recently chose.
      assign up_recent = cart.items | reverse
      for up_item in up_recent limit: 3
        if up_handle != blank
          break
        endif
        capture up_try
          render 'cartel-pick-collection', source: up_item.product, count: up_want, deny: up_deny
        endcapture
        assign up_handle = up_try | strip
      endfor
    endif

    # Two steps: a filter cannot be applied inside a bracket lookup.
    assign up_key = up_handle | strip
    assign up_coll = collections[up_key]
  -%}
  {%- if up_coll != blank -%}
    {%- liquid
      # One delimited string instead of a nested scan per candidate — same trick
      # as main-cart-items.liquid:497. Commas on both ends make it an exact id
      # match, so 123 cannot match inside 1234.
      assign up_pids = cart.items | map: 'product' | map: 'id' | join: ',' | prepend: ',' | append: ','
      assign up_n = 0
    -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Captured because the wrapper must not be emitted when nothing qualifies —
      an empty bordered strip with a heading is worse than no strip.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture up_cards -%}
      {%- for up_p in up_coll.products limit: 12 -%}
        {%- if up_n >= up_want -%}
          {%- break -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign up_pid = up_p.id | prepend: ',' | append: ','
          assign up_v = up_p.selected_or_first_available_variant
          assign up_ok = true

          # already in the bag
          if up_pids contains up_pid
            assign up_ok = false
          endif
          # nothing to add
          if up_p.available == false
            assign up_ok = false
          endif
          # "Price on request" SKUs route to /pages/contact (cartel-card.liquid:75).
          # That is an enquiry, not an impulse add — it cannot pay for a slot here.
          if up_v.price == 0
            assign up_ok = false
          endif
          # Thuya is login-gated. A card that can only say "Log in to see price"
          # cannot convert, and the footer's .dw-lock already explains the gate.
          if up_p.vendor == 'Thuya' and customer == nil
            assign up_ok = false
          endif

          if up_ok
            assign up_n = up_n | plus: 1
            render 'cartel-drawer-upsell-card', card_product: up_p
          endif
        -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if up_n > 0 -%}
      <div class="dw-up">
        {%- comment -%}
          h3, not h2: the dialog's own name is the h2.dw-title "Your bag (n)".
          Card names below are spans, not headings — three more headings would
          bury "Your bag" in a screen reader's heading list. role="list" is
          explicit because display:flex on a list-style:none <ul> drops list
          semantics in Safari/VoiceOver.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <h3 class="dw-up-h" id="CartDrawer-UpsellHeading">You may also like</h3>
        <ul class="dw-up-rail" role="list" aria-labelledby="CartDrawer-UpsellHeading">
          {{ up_cards }}
        </ul>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
